{"action":"IMPLEMENT","change_name":"cycle-11-pipe-od-retrieval-normalization","hypothesis":"A guarded, standards-backed outer-pipe-diameter-to-DN retrieval alternate will improve candidate recall for valve tenders that specify an unambiguous pipe OD rather than DN, while preserving original-query reranking and selection.","why_now":"The current canonicalizer handles compact DN/PN and notation but explicitly declines bare pipe OD. The taxonomy identifies this as the remaining parser miss, and external technical evidence confirms the common OD 108 mm / DN 100 relationship for welded steel pipe. This is a new query-time representation experiment, not an unsafe alias or selection change.","expected_effect":"Add at most one DN-enriched retrieval query only when a supported valve-family query has a clear pipe-OD marker, no explicit DN, and a documented mapping; leave the original retrieval, reranker input, and output unchanged.","expected_metric_gain":"+0–3.3 pp public hard-pass and +0–3.3 pp blind hard-pass; the primary benefit is resolving a documented parser class with low safety risk.","lesson_from_history":"Selection-adjacent changes regressed or were neutral (cycles 1, 2, 5, 6, and 8), whereas additive query canonicalization was the only accepted mechanism (cycles 3–4). Cycle 10 was blocked by a protected-file contract violation before evaluation, so it is inconclusive rather than evidence against schema work. Catalog enrichment regressed (cycle 7), so this avoids an index rebuild.","candidate_hypotheses":["Guarded pipe-OD-to-DN additive retrieval normalization for standard pipe sizes (selected).","Corrected, protected-file-safe flange-subtype requirement modeling, revisiting the inconclusive cycle-10 implementation protocol failure.","Subject-matter-validated legacy designation equivalence mappings for Soviet/vendor valve codes.","Hybrid candidate-depth or RRF tuning without an evidenced retrieval miss."],"needs_reindex":false,"plan_summary":"I have selected a query-time parser/canonicalization experiment and am creating the required OpenSpec artifacts only.","used_external_research":true,"research_sources":["https://meganorm.ru/mega_doc/norm/gost_gosudarstvennyj-standart/0/gost_10704-91_mezhgosudarstvennyy_standart_truby_stalnye.html","https://tavago.ru/truby-i-fitingi/stalnye-truby/truby-stalnye-elektrosvarnye-gost-10704-91/truba-stal-elektrosvarnaya-pryamoshovnaya-dn-108kh3-5-du-100-gost-10704-91.html"],"research_summary":"The GOST 10704-91 source lists 108 mm as a standardized outside diameter, and the pipe product source identifies DN 108×3.5 as DN 100. This supports a narrowly documented mapping only for explicit outer-diameter context, not general numeric conversion."}
