index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..6c12da5d6ef357a73aee87dd39cf23cee0d8075e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/openspec/changes/cycle-11-pipe-od-retrieval-normalization/specs/pipe-od-retrieval-normalization/spec.md
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+## Purpose
+
+Provide a conservative catalog-native size representation when a supported valve tender specifies a standard pipe outside diameter instead of an explicit nominal diameter.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Produce a guarded OD-to-DN retrieval alternate
+
+For a supported valve-family tender that has no explicit DN, the system SHALL provide at most one additional retrieval representation when it contains exactly one explicit pipe-diameter cue and that OD occurs in the approved standards-backed mapping table. The alternate SHALL retain the source wording and all explicit product, pressure, material, connection, control, designation, and construction terms while adding the mapped DN term. The original normalized tender query SHALL remain available for original retrieval, reranking, and returned result text.
+
+#### Scenario: Standard pipe OD in a valve tender
+
+- **WHEN** a supported valve tender without an explicit DN contains a single recognized pipe-OD expression for an approved OD value
+- **THEN** the system provides one distinct alternate representation that retains the OD expression and adds its mapped DN
+
+#### Scenario: Explicit DN takes precedence
+
+- **WHEN** a supported valve tender contains both an explicit DN and a recognized pipe-OD expression
+- **THEN** the system does not derive or add a second DN from the OD expression
+
+### Requirement: Refuse ambiguous diameter conversion
+
+The system SHALL NOT infer DN from a bare number, a non-pipe dimension, multiple competing diameter expressions, an OD value outside the approved table, or an unsupported/no-product query. When no other existing canonicalization applies, it SHALL not emit an OD-derived alternate query.
+
+#### Scenario: Unmapped or ambiguous dimension
+
+- **WHEN** a tender has an unapproved OD, more than one possible pipe diameter, or a dimension without an explicit supported OD cue
+- **THEN** the system does not add a DN term based on that dimension
+
+#### Scenario: Unsupported product text
+
+- **WHEN** an unsupported or no-product query contains an OD-like number with millimetres
+- **THEN** the system does not create a catalog-domain DN alternate on that basis
+
+### Requirement: Keep OD expansion additive and fail-open
+
+The system SHALL use an OD-derived representation only as an additional retrieval input, at most once per query, and SHALL retain usable original-query candidates if alternate retrieval is unavailable or fails. It SHALL not add duplicate candidates or extra retrieval-modality scoring solely because a result appears through both source and OD-derived representations.
+
+#### Scenario: Alternate retrieval failure
+
+- **WHEN** retrieval of the OD-derived representation fails after original-query retrieval succeeds
+- **THEN** matching continues with the original-query candidate set

