+## 1. Guarded OD Recognition
+
+- [ ] 1.1 Extend the query-time canonicalization boundary with the documented exact `108 mm -> DN 100` allowlist and contextual OD recognition; verify a synthetic supported flanged or welded valve request with one millimetre-qualified OD and no DN produces one source-preserving DN-enriched alternate.
+- [ ] 1.2 Enforce refusal rules for explicit DN, unapproved OD values, bare/unqualified dimensions, multiple competing dimensions, and unsupported/no-product text; verify focused unit tests assert that none gains an OD-derived DN term.
+
+## 2. Regression Coverage
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Add focused synthetic tests in the canonicalization test module covering concise `d ... мм`, explicit outer/pipe diameter wording, retention of PN/construction/designation terms, and the existing source-query contract; verify `python -m pytest tests/test_query_canonicalization.py -q` passes.
+- [ ] 2.2 Confirm the canonicalization result remains a single optional alternate and does not require matcher or hybrid-retriever API, RRF, reranker, index, catalog, or GOLD/harness changes; verify existing hybrid/matcher tests pass unchanged.
+
+## 3. Verification
+
+- [ ] 3.1 Run `python -m pytest -q` and resolve product-code or focused-test failures while keeping edits restricted to query-time canonicalization and its focused tests.

